    "tablehtml": "<h1><u>Corrigenda</u></h1>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><em><span style=\"font-size: 16.0pt; line-height: 107%;\">WHO Classification of Tumours, 5th edition:<br />Central Nervous System Tumours</span></em></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Most recent corrigenda update to this volume online: <span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">21 Nov 2022</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h1>Summary of corrections:</h1>\r\n<h2><span style=\"color: black;\">Astrocytoma, IDH-mutant (p.&nbsp;19)</span></h2>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\">In the print version, a reference citation has been added at the end of the <em>Localization</em> subsection as shown. In the online version, an incorrect PMID had previously been cited here and has now been corrected as shown.</p>\r\n<table class=\"MsoTableGrid\" style=\"width: 487.1pt; border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"1\" width=\"649\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DEEAF6; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Original text (print)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-left: none; background: #DEEAF6; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Corrected text (print)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-top: none; padding: 7.1pt 5.4pt 7.1pt 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><strong>Localization</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\">&hellip; A genetically distinct form of IDH-mutant astrocytoma has recently been described in the infratentorial compartment.</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border-top: none; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-right: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 7.1pt 5.4pt 7.1pt 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><strong>Localization</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\">&hellip; A genetically distinct form of IDH-mutant astrocytoma has recently been described in the infratentorial compartment <span style=\"color: #c00000; background: #D9D9D9;\">(187)</span>.</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-top: none; background: #DEEAF6; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Original text (online)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border-top: none; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-right: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DEEAF6; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Corrected text (online)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-top: none; padding: 7.1pt 5.4pt 7.1pt 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><strong>Localization</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\">&hellip; A genetically distinct form of IDH-mutant astrocytoma has recently been described in the infratentorial compartment <span style=\"color: #c00000; background: #D9D9D9;\">(1897)</span>.</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border-top: none; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-right: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 7.1pt 5.4pt 7.1pt 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><strong>Localization</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\">&hellip; A genetically distinct form of IDH-mutant astrocytoma has recently been described in the infratentorial compartment <span style=\"color: #c00000; background: #D9D9D9;\">(187)</span>.</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 487.1pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-top: none; padding: 7.1pt 5.4pt 7.1pt 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"649\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt;\">References cited above:</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt;\">187.</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt;\"> Banan R, Stichel D, Bleck A, et al. Infratentorial IDH-mutant astrocytoma is a distinct subtype. Acta Neuropathol. 2020 Oct;140(4):569&ndash;81. PMID: {32776277}</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt;\">1897.</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt;\"> Lin KM, Lin SJ, Lin JH, et al. Dysregulation of dual-specificity phosphatases by Epstein-Barr virus LMP1 and its impact on lymphoblastoid cell line survival. J Virol. 2020 Jan 31;94(4):e01837-19. </span><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt;\">PMID: {31776277}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; line-height: 107%;\">Updated online: Yes, in most recent corrigenda update<br />Updated in print: Yes (in 3rd print run), November 2022</span></p>\r\n<h2><span style=\"color: black;\">Astrocytoma, IDH-mutant (p.&nbsp;26)</span></h2>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\">The &ldquo;greater than&rdquo; symbol has been corrected to a &ldquo;greater than or equal to&rdquo; symbol as shown.</p>\r\n<table class=\"MsoTableGrid\" style=\"width: 487.1pt; border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"1\" width=\"649\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DEEAF6; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Original text</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-left: none; background: #DEEAF6; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Corrected text</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-top: none; padding: 7.1pt 5.4pt 7.1pt 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><strong>Diagnostic molecular pathology</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\">&hellip;</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; text-indent: 8.2pt; line-height: normal;\">Immunohistochemical staining for [&hellip;]</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><em>[top of p. 26:]</em></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\">helps to distinguish true neoplasia from [&hellip;]. Given the low frequency of <em>IDH1</em> and <em>IDH2</em> mutations in CNS WHO grade&nbsp;4 gliomas arising in patients aged <span style=\"color: #c00000; background: #D9D9D9;\">&gt;</span>&nbsp;55&nbsp;years, sequencing analysis need not follow a negative IDH1 p.R132H immunostain in this patient population.</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border-top: none; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-right: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 7.1pt 5.4pt 7.1pt 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><strong>Diagnostic molecular pathology</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\">&hellip;</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; text-indent: 8.2pt; line-height: normal;\">Immunohistochemical staining for [&hellip;]</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><em>[top of p. 26:]</em></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\">helps to distinguish true neoplasia from [&hellip;]. Given the low frequency of <em>IDH1</em> and <em>IDH2</em> mutations in CNS WHO grade&nbsp;4 gliomas arising in patients aged <span style=\"color: #c00000; background: #D9D9D9;\">&ge;</span>&nbsp;55&nbsp;years, sequencing analysis need not follow a negative IDH1 p.R132H immunostain in this patient population.</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; line-height: 107%;\">Updated online: Yes, in most recent corrigenda update<br />Updated in print: Yes (in 3rd print run), November 2022</span></p>\r\n<h2><span style=\"color: black;\">Posterior fossa group A (PFA) ependymoma (p.&nbsp;174)</span></h2>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\">The final sentence of the <em>Prognosis and prediction</em> subsection has been corrected as shown.</p>\r\n<table class=\"MsoTableGrid\" style=\"width: 487.1pt; border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"1\" width=\"649\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DEEAF6; padding: 0cm 4.25pt 0cm 4.25pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Original text</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-left: none; background: #DEEAF6; padding: 0cm 4.25pt 0cm 4.25pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Corrected text</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-top: none; padding: 7.1pt 4.25pt 7.1pt 4.25pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Prognosis and prediction</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\">&hellip; The prognostic significance of an H3 <span style=\"color: #c00000; background: #D9D9D9;\">p.K28me3</span> (<span style=\"color: #c00000; background: #D9D9D9;\">K27me3</span>) mutation in a small proportion of PFA ependymomas is unknown.</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border-top: none; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-right: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 7.1pt 4.25pt 7.1pt 4.25pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Prognosis and prediction</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\">&hellip; The prognostic significance of an H3 <span style=\"color: #c00000; background: #D9D9D9;\">p.K28</span> (<span style=\"color: #c00000; background: #D9D9D9;\">K27</span>)&nbsp;mutation in a small proportion of PFA ependymomas is unknown <span style=\"color: #c00000; background: #D9D9D9;\">(1065,2765)</span>.</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 11.7pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 487.1pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-top: none; padding: 7.1pt 5.4pt 7.1pt 5.4pt; height: 11.7pt;\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"649\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt;\">References added above:</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt;\">1065.</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt;\"> Gessi M, Capper D, Sahm F, et al. Evidence of H3 K27M mutations in posterior fossa ependymomas. Acta Neuropathol. 2016 Oct;132(4):635&ndash;7. PMID:&nbsp;{27539613}</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt;\">2765.</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt;\"> Ryall S, Guzman M, Elbabaa SK, et al. H3 K27M mutations are extremely rare in posterior fossa group A ependymoma. Childs Nerv Syst. 2017 Jul;33(7):1047&ndash;51. PMID: {28623522}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; line-height: 107%;\">Updated online: Yes, in most recent corrigenda update<br />Updated in print: Yes (in 2nd print run), February 2022</span></p>\r\n<h2><span style=\"color: black;\">Myxopapillary ependymoma (p.&nbsp;184)</span></h2>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\">&ldquo;&ge;&nbsp;2&nbsp;mitoses/mm<sup>2</sup>&rdquo; has been corrected to &ldquo;&ge;&nbsp;5&nbsp;mitoses/mm<sup>2</sup>&rdquo; as shown.</p>\r\n<table class=\"MsoTableGrid\" style=\"width: 487.1pt; border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"1\" width=\"649\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DEEAF6; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Original text</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-left: none; background: #DEEAF6; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Corrected text</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-top: none; padding: 7.1pt 5.4pt 7.1pt 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Histopathology</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\">&hellip;</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\"><em>[top of p. 184:]</em></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\">by PAS and Alcian blue positivity [&hellip;]. Exceptional examples termed &ldquo;anaplastic myxopapillary ependymomas&rdquo; manifest regional hypercellularity and reduced mucin in association with at least two of the following features: &ge;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: #c00000; background: #D9D9D9;\">2</span>&nbsp;mitoses/mm<sup>2</sup>, Ki-67 labelling index &ge;&nbsp;10%, microvascular proliferation, and spontaneous necrosis &hellip;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border-top: none; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-right: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 7.1pt 5.4pt 7.1pt 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Histopathology</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\">&hellip;</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\"><em>[top of p. 184:]</em></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\">by PAS and Alcian blue positivity [&hellip;]. Exceptional examples termed &ldquo;anaplastic myxopapillary ependymomas&rdquo; manifest regional hypercellularity and reduced mucin in association with at least two of the following features: &ge;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: #c00000; background: #D9D9D9;\">5</span>&nbsp;mitoses/mm<sup>2</sup>, Ki-67 labelling index &ge;&nbsp;10%, microvascular proliferation, and spontaneous necrosis &hellip;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; line-height: 107%;\">Updated online: Yes, in most recent corrigenda update<br />Updated in print: Yes (in 3rd print run), November 2022</span></p>\r\n<h2><span style=\"color: black;\">Primary diffuse large B-cell lymphoma of the CNS (p.&nbsp;351)</span></h2>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\">A minor typographical error has been corrected as shown.</p>\r\n<table class=\"MsoTableGrid\" style=\"width: 487.1pt; border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"1\" width=\"649\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DEEAF6; padding: 0cm 4.25pt 0cm 4.25pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Original text</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-left: none; background: #DEEAF6; padding: 0cm 4.25pt 0cm 4.25pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Corrected text</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-top: none; padding: 7.1pt 4.25pt 7.1pt 4.25pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Localization</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\">Primary CNS-DLB<span style=\"color: #c00000; background: #D9D9D9;\">LC</span>s are solitary brain lesions in 65% of cases &hellip;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border-top: none; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-right: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 7.1pt 4.25pt 7.1pt 4.25pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Localization</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\">Primary CNS-DLB<span style=\"color: #c00000; background: #D9D9D9;\">CL</span>s are solitary brain lesions in 65% of cases &hellip;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; line-height: 107%;\">Updated online: Yes, in most recent corrigenda update<br />Updated in print: Yes (in 3rd print run), November 2022</span></p>\r\n<h2><span style=\"color: black;\">Germ cell tumours of the CNS (p.&nbsp;384)</span></h2>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\">A reference citation has been corrected as shown.</p>\r\n<table class=\"MsoTableGrid\" style=\"width: 487.1pt; border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"1\" width=\"649\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DEEAF6; padding: 0cm 4.25pt 0cm 4.25pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Original text</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-left: none; background: #DEEAF6; padding: 0cm 4.25pt 0cm 4.25pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Corrected text</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-top: none; padding: 7.1pt 4.25pt 7.1pt 4.25pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Etiology</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\">Germline variants of the <em>JMJD1C</em> gene, which encodes a jumonji domain&ndash;containing histone demethylase, have been associated with a heightened risk of CNS germ cell tumours in Japanese people <span style=\"color: #c00000; background: #D9D9D9;\">(1762)</span>.</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border-top: none; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-right: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 7.1pt 4.25pt 7.1pt 4.25pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Etiology</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\">Germline variants of the <em>JMJD1C</em> gene, which encodes a jumonji domain&ndash;containing histone demethylase, have been associated with a heightened risk of CNS germ cell tumours in Japanese people <span style=\"color: #c00000; background: #D9D9D9;\">(3374)</span>.</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 487.1pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-top: none; padding: 7.1pt 5.4pt 7.1pt 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"649\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt;\">References cited above:</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt;\">1762.</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt;\"> Kuroki S, Akiyoshi M, Tokura M, et al. JMJD1C, a JmjC domain-containing protein, is required for long-term maintenance of male germ cells in mice. Biol Reprod. 2013 Oct 17;89(4):93. PMID: {24006281}</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt;\">3374.</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt;\"> Wang L, Yamaguchi S, Burstein MD, et al. Novel somatic and germline mutations in intracranial germ cell tumours. Nature. 2014 Jul 10;511(7508):241&ndash;5. </span><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt;\">PMID: {24896186}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; line-height: 107%;\">Updated online: Yes, in most recent corrigenda update<br />Updated in print: Yes (in 3rd print run), November 2022</span></p>\r\n<h2><span style=\"color: black;\">Adamantinomatous craniopharyngioma (p.&nbsp;394, 396)</span></h2>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\">&ldquo;Xp28&rdquo; has been corrected to &ldquo;Xq28&rdquo; as shown.</p>\r\n<table class=\"MsoTableGrid\" style=\"width: 487.1pt; border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"1\" width=\"649\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DEEAF6; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Original text</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-left: none; background: #DEEAF6; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Corrected text</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-top: none; padding: 7.1pt 5.4pt 7.1pt 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><strong>Pathogenesis</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\">&hellip;</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; text-indent: 8.2pt; line-height: normal;\">Adamantinomatous craniopharyngiomas are characterized by [&hellip;]. Recurrent focal deletions of X<span style=\"color: #c00000; background: #D9D9D9;\">p</span>28 have been described in a subset of samples from male patients, and other recurrent gains have also been described &hellip;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border-top: none; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-right: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 7.1pt 5.4pt 7.1pt 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><strong>Pathogenesis</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\">&hellip;</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\">Adamantinomatous craniopharyngiomas are characterized by [&hellip;]. Recurrent focal deletions of X<span style=\"color: #c00000; background: #D9D9D9;\">q</span>28 have been described in a subset of samples from male patients, and other recurrent gains have also been described &hellip;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-top: none; padding: 7.1pt 5.4pt 7.1pt 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><strong>Prognosis and prediction</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\">&hellip;</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; text-indent: 8.2pt; line-height: normal;\">Overall survival rates [&hellip;]. Although there are few studies of molecular features predictive of worse outcome, tumours with <em>CTNNB1</em> p .T41 mutations or focal deletions of X<span style=\"color: #c00000; background: #D9D9D9;\">p</span>28 may be associated with a worse outcome &hellip;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 243.55pt; border-top: none; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-right: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 7.1pt 5.4pt 7.1pt 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"325\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><strong>Prognosis and prediction</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\">&hellip;</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\">Overall survival rates [&hellip;]. Although there are few studies of molecular features predictive of worse outcome, tumours with <em>CTNNB1</em> p .T41 mutations or focal deletions of X<span style=\"color: #c00000; background: #D9D9D9;\">q</span>28 may be associated with a worse outcome &hellip;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; line-height: 107%;\">Updated online: Yes, in most recent corrigenda update<br />Updated in print: Yes (in 3rd print run), November 2022</span></p>",
